      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Let us find the different ways so that&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn></math>&nbsp;persons can travel in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math>&nbsp;cars.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable columnlines=\"solid solid none\" rowlines=\"solid solid solid none\"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>3</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>3</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>2</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>2</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>3</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>3</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>3</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>2</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>3</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p><p>Hence we have&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math>&nbsp;ways.</p><p>Now the number of ways to distribute&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn></math>&nbsp;persons such that they can travel in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math>&nbsp;cars with any car carrying maximum of&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math>&nbsp;persons is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>!</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>!</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>!</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>1680</mn></math></p><p>Therefore, the required answer is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1680</mn></math></p></blockquote>",
    "image": null
  },
